# The endpoints that hold an Apache worker rather than merely costing CPU.
# /socialauth/ is the worst: it makes an OUTBOUND call to Google per request, so
# each one occupies a worker while blocked off-box — which is why the machine
# shows load 0.00 with every worker busy. /feedback/, /search/ and
# /accounts/register/ are the other expensive targets seen in the 2026-09-17
# incident. robots.txt already disallows all four for every crawler.
#
# /accounts/register only, not all of /accounts/: /accounts/login/ is how real
# readers sign in. See regluit-flood.conf for the line shape.
#
# Managed by Ansible (regluit_prod). EbookFoundation/security-private#32.
[Definition]
failregex = ^<HOST> \[[^\]]*\] "(?:GET|POST|HEAD|PUT|PATCH|DELETE|OPTIONS) /(?:feedback|search|socialauth|accounts/register)(?=[/?\s])
ignoreregex =
